  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Stamp of Origin",
    "overview": "The north star is the owner's chosen direction recorded in ADR-0006: stencilled produce crates and the rubber stamps of origin and grade on them, translated into a working interface for a shopper at the stall, on a phone. The world is ultramarine stamp ink on near-white label paper, stencil-black text, condensed heavy capitals for names, headings and stamps, and a plain humanist sans for everything that is read or operated. Stamp red is spent on one thing, the „Разгар“ (peak) level, and one marker yellow is reserved for the current month in the footer's month links. Dark mode is its own scale, a deep ink-blue ground with lighter stamp inks, not an inversion.\n\nThe world is calm by decision. Capitals appear only in the logo, headings and stamps, the surfaces are flat, separation comes from hairline rules, and there is no motion beyond the global reduced-motion guard. Density is moderate on reading pages (content column capped at 72rem, prose at 42rem, sections 2–4rem apart) and deliberately compact in the in-season list, which fits about ten rows on the first screen of a phone.\n\nThis file describes the system as built after spec 024 (#93): the tokens and typography (spec 022), the shell header and footer (spec 023, #92), and the season stamp, year strip, legend and in-season list (spec 024). The produce page (#94) and the data visuals (#95) still carry their earlier layouts in the new tokens; anything marked **planned** is decided in ADR-0006 but not yet in the code. Tokens are generated from `src/design/tokens.ts` and inlined as CSS custom properties (`--color-*`, `--space-*`, `--font-size-*`, `--radius-*`, and others); light values sit on `:root` and dark values override them under `prefers-color-scheme: dark`. Print uses its own `--print-*` set from `src/styles/base.css` (black ink on white paper).",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Sofia Sans Extra Condensed 800 in capitals for the logo, headings and stamps; Sofia Sans for body, navigation, lists and tables.",
      "Latin names in Sofia Sans italic 400, through the global `[lang='la']` rule.",
      "Ultramarine ink on label paper; stamp red only for „Разгар“; marker yellow only for the current month.",
      "The season level is carried by form and word: a solid, outlined or hatched stamp with its short Bulgarian word, and the same three forms in the year strip. Never colour alone.",
      "Flat surfaces and hairline rules, no shadows, no motion.",
      "One small corner radius (0.375rem) on panels and controls; stamps and strip cells are square-cornered.",
      "Touch targets of at least 2.75rem on primary links and controls; at least 24px in compact list rows."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Red Means Разгар Rule",
        "body": "Stamp red is the „Разгар“ level and nothing else: not errors, not links, not emphasis. Text on it is always `on-peak`.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Marker Rule",
        "body": "Marker yellow marks the current month and nothing else. It is a fill with `on-marker` text, never a line or a text colour on the light page.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tested Pair Rule",
        "body": "A colour is used on a background only when that pair is in the tested contrast set. Components take colours from tokens only and contain no literal colours.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Capitals Are Headings Rule",
        "body": "Sofia Sans Extra Condensed in capitals is for the logo, `h1`–`h3` and the season stamps. Capitals come from `text-transform`, so the source text and reading order are unchanged without CSS. Body, navigation, lists and tables stay in Sofia Sans, in sentence case.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Weight Rule",
        "body": "The condensed face exists at 800 only. Never set it at another weight or in italic; the browser would synthesise it.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every table uses `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink On Paper Rule",
